Applying the network policy made no apparent change; but when the load balancer is created a new firewall is created and can be seen in the console under network security >> firewall policies >> vpc firewall rules.  It allows ingress to the Load Balancer external IP from 0.0.0.0/0 on the port specified (7777 for us).  If you modify that firewall rule to only allow traffic from the external IP of the VM running the nginx proxy and configure the proxy for the LB IP/port then you can access the API from the proxied url and not from the LB IP directly. 
